"""Predict a consonant-heavy join between spelling fragments.

Short lower-case fragments after a vowel-bearing, consonant-ending piece get
positive values, with extra strength for trailing consonant clusters and stop
letters. Case and vowel content distinguish ordinary word pieces from acronyms
and consonant-only pieces. Other positions stay near zero. A document-initial
Title: metadata label has its own strong response, especially on the colon.

