HAR is strongly negative, HARD stronger still. This is a spelling rule, not a
rule for every word containing those letters: long words and CH/SH/PH digraphs
usually weaken it. Some short HI/HU syllables are positive instead. Alphabet
transliteration extends the same rules beyond Latin. There are also small
rules for the Chinese hard/ha characters and repeated middle dots.
