Headings, bullets, code introductions, and digits tend to give large positive
responses. Most ordinary text gives much less. An initial run of identical
tokens keeps the opening response; later text is silent apart from `Title:`
and the second line of an opening // comment. These coarse classes deliberately
omit the component's many word-specific differences.
