The strongest negative response is to another m-initial word part inside an
m-initial word (mer + maid), followed by adjacent m-initial words. Smaller
negative terms cover repeated m's and their continuing suffixes. There is a
separate document-initial offset, and a strong positive response to the colon
in a document-opening 'Title:'. Everything is computed incrementally and reset
at document boundaries; no vocabulary lookup table is used.
