"""A surface approximation to an end-of-enclosure signal.

It recognizes closing brackets, quotations, inline code, math and emphasis.
Tightly attached closures are stronger than whitespace-separated closures;
a comma, period or newline fused to the token usually suppresses the signal.
Angle-bracketed types and NUL-separated text are additional formatting cases.
Document starts get a negative offset, especially for short fragments.
Small rules also recognize LaTeX right, Python from/import, and dot fill.
State tracks paired quote/markup delimiters, not the model's hidden state.
